# Load-bearing text the privacy check (ADR 0013) would otherwise flag, one Python regex per line, each passed as
# --privacy-allow by tools/validate/homelab-validate and CI (.github/workflows/validate.yaml) through
# validate_paths.py. A denylisted match is exempt only when it lies wholly inside a match of one of these.
# Keep each as narrow as the text it exempts; prose that merely mentions a name is generalized instead.
#
# Install commands, which must name the repository they install from.
git\+https://github\.com/[\w.-]+/[\w.-]+@[\w.-]+#subdirectory=[\w./-]+
# A release download in a runbook command (host/README.md).
https://github\.com/[\w.-]+/[\w.-]+/releases/download/\S+
# The Grafana folder and tag of the provisioned dashboards, a string literal alone on its line in dashboards.py.
^"home-ops"$
